1
00:04:39,000 --> 00:04:45,000
Beyond Sherwood Forest is a action, adventure,
fantasy film directed by Peter DeLuise.

2
00:09:18,000 --> 00:09:24,000
King Richard is away fighting the Crusade, his brother
Prince John has been left in charge.

3
00:13:57,000 --> 00:14:03,000
In order to further international diplomatic relations with Norway, the
beautiful young Maid Marian is to be married off to a prince.

4
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:42,000
A cursed girl who can change into a ferocious dragon
is used to find and pacify Robin Hood.

5
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:21,000
Little John, played by Mark Gibbon.

6
00:27:54,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Friar Tuck, played by Bill Dow.

7
00:32:33,000 --> 00:32:39,000
Malcolm, played by Julian Sands.

8
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:18,000
Will Scarlet, played by Richard de Klerk.

9
00:41:51,000 --> 00:41:57,000
Robin Hood, played by Robin Dunne.

10
00:46:30,000 --> 00:46:36,000
Alina, played by Katharine Isabelle.

11
00:51:09,000 --> 00:51:15,000
Sherwood Forest consists of the remnants of an ancient Royal Forest in
Nottinghamshire, in the East Midlands region of England.

12
00:55:48,000 --> 00:55:54,000
It is associated with the legend of Robin Hood.

13
01:00:27,000 --> 01:00:33,000
The forest was proclaimed by William the Conqueror and
mentioned in the Domesday Book in 1086.

14
01:05:06,000 --> 01:05:12,000
The reserve has the highest concentration of ancient trees in Europe.

15
01:09:45,000 --> 01:09:51,000
Today, Sherwood Forest National Nature Reserve encompasses 424.75 hectares (1,049.6
acres), surrounding the village of Edwinstowe and the site of Thoresby Hall.

16
01:14:24,000 --> 01:14:30,000
The reserve contains more than a thousand ancient oaks which are known to be
more than 500 years old, with the Major Oak being twice that age.

17
01:19:03,000 --> 01:19:09,000
Sherwood Forest is within an area which used to be called "Birch
Lund", which is Viking in origin, now known as Birklands.

18
01:23:42,000 --> 01:23:48,000
The oak trees from Sherwood Forest were used to build the roof of St Paul's
Cathedral in London and 1st Viscount Nelson's naval fleet.

19
01:28:21,000 --> 01:28:27,000
The film explores themes of robin hood, arrow, friar, arch, 12th century.
